<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Simplify Expressions Using the Distributive Property: Mini-Lesson Review</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01545</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Simplify Expressions Using the Distributive Property: Mini-Lesson Review</md:title>
    <md:uuid>5b8ca2e6-d0f0-4739-b59d-fe07de52ca84</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <note class="mini-lesson-question" id="note-00003">
        <title>Question #2: Simplify Expressions Using the Distributive Property</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Which expression is equivalent to <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math>?</para>
      </note>
    </section>

    <section id="sect-00002">
      <title>Simplify Expressions Using the Distributive Property</title>
      <para id="para-00002">The Distributive Property can be used to remove parentheses as you
        simplify expressions.</para>
      <note id="note-00001">
        <para id="para-00003">
          <emphasis> DISTRIBUTIVE PROPERTY</emphasis>
        </para>
        
        <para id="para-00004"><m:math display="block">
            <m:semantics>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mrow>
                  <m:mtable>
                    <m:mtr>
                      <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                        <m:mtext>If</m:mtext>
                        <m:mspace width="0.2em"/>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>,</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                        <m:mspace width="0.2em"/>
                        <m:mtext>are real numbers, then</m:mtext>
                      </m:mtd>
                      <m:mtd/>
                      <m:mtd/>
                      <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                        <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                        <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                      </m:mtd>
                    </m:mtr>
                    <m:mtr/>
                    <m:mtr/>
                    <m:mtr>
                      <m:mtd columnalign="right">
                        <m:mtext>Also,</m:mtext>
                      </m:mtd>
                      <m:mtd/>
                      <m:mtd/>
                      <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      </m:mtd>
                    </m:mtr>
                    <m:mtr>
                      <m:mtd/>
                      <m:mtd/>
                      <m:mtd/>
                      <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                        <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                        <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                      </m:mtd>
                    </m:mtr>
                    <m:mtr>
                      <m:mtd/>
                      <m:mtd/>
                      <m:mtd/>
                      <m:mtd columnalign="left">
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                        <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>=</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>b</m:mi>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                        <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                        <m:mi>c</m:mi>
                        <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                      </m:mtd>
                    </m:mtr>
                  </m:mtable>
                </m:mrow>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:semantics>
          </m:math></para></note>

      <para id="para-00005">Simplify:</para>
      <para id="para-00024">1. <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mi>x</m:mi>
              <m:mo>+</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00025">It may help to
          use arrows to show the Distributive Property.</para>
          <media alt="">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_02_06_01.jpg"/>
          </media>
          <para id="para-00026">Use the Distributive Property.</para>
          <para id="para-00027">
            <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>⋅</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>⋅</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn>
            </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
          </para>
          <para id="para-00028">Multiply.</para>
          <para id="para-00029">
            <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn>
                <m:mi>x</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>12</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
          </para>

      <para id="para-00030">2. <m:math display="inline">
            <m:mrow>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>11</m:mn>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
              <m:mn>4</m:mn>
              <m:mo>−</m:mo>
              <m:mn>3</m:mn>
              <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
            </m:mrow>
          </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00031">Use arrows to
          show the Distributive Property.</para>
          <media alt="">
            <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_02_06_02.jpg"/>
          </media>
          <para id="para-00032">Use the Distributive Property</para>
          <para id="para-00033">
            <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>-</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mo>⋅</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>-</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>-</m:mo><m:mn>11</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>⋅</m:mo>
                <m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
          </para>
          <para id="para-00034">Multiply.</para>
          <para id="para-00035">
            <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>-</m:mo><m:mn>44</m:mn><m:mo>-</m:mo><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>-</m:mo><m:mn>33</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
          </para>
          <para id="para-00036">Simplify.</para>
          <para id="para-00037">
            <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>-</m:mo><m:mn>44</m:mn><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>33</m:mn><m:mi>a</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>
          </para>
          <para id="para-00038">Watch signs when using the Distributive Property with negative signs.</para>
    </section>

    <note class="try" id="note-00002"><title>Try It: Simplify Expressions Using the Distributive
      Property </title>
        <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00006">Simplify: <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>.</para>
          <para id="para-00007">Write down your answer. Then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis>
      button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00008">Here is how to simplify expressions using the Distributive Property.</para>
          <para id="para-00009">Use arrows to show the Distributive Property.</para>
          <para id="para-00010">
            <media alt="">
              <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_07_02_06_03.jpg"/>
            </media>

          </para>
          <para id="para-00011">Use the Distributive Property. <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
                <m:mi>·</m:mi>
                <m:mn>1</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00012">Multiply. <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00013">Simplify. <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                <m:mi>y</m:mi>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </note>
    <section class="check-understanding" id="sect-00003">
      <title>Check Your Understanding</title>
      <exercise id="fe2725a9-e34e-4c6a-ba93-4368602af0de" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00002">
          <para id="para-00014">Which expression is equivalent to <m:math display="inline">
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>4</m:mn>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo>
                <m:mn>5</m:mn>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
                <m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math>?</para>
          <para id="para-00015">Multiple Choice:</para>
          <para id="para-00016"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>20</m:mn>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00017"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>20</m:mn>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>2</m:mn>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00018"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>20</m:mn>
                <m:mo>−</m:mo>
                <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
          <para id="para-00019"><m:math>
              <m:mrow>
                <m:mn>20</m:mn>
                <m:mo>+</m:mo>
                <m:mn>8</m:mn>
                <m:mi>a</m:mi>
              </m:mrow>
            </m:math></para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00002">
          <para id="para-00020">Correct! Check yourself: Multiply the factor outside the parentheses
            by each term inside the parentheses.</para>
          <para id="para-00021">Try again. Let’s try again a different way: To use the Distributive
            Property, multiply the factor outside the parentheses by each term inside the
            parentheses.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
    <section id="sect-00004">
      <title>Videos </title>
      <para id="para-00022">Watch the first 2 minutes and 40 seconds of the video to see how to use
        the Distributive Property to simplify expressions.</para>
      <para id="para-00023">
        <emphasis>Khan Academy: Distributive property with variables</emphasis>
      </para>
      <media alt="Placeholder for Alt Text">
        <iframe width="660" height="371.4" src="https://www.youtube-nocookie.com/embed/Jp25LHI9wII;&amp;rel=0"/>
      </media>
    </section>
  </content>
